WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.880
During the '90s and early 2000s, it seemed
like Edward Norton was pretty much everywhere.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:09.999
He took roles in a wide range of classic movies,
including Fight Club, American History X,

00:00:09.999 --> 00:00:14.809
Kingdom of Heaven, Red Dragon and The Illusionist,
and was beloved by fans almost as much as

00:00:14.809 --> 00:00:16.160
he was lauded by critics.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:20.530
In recent years, however, it feels like he's
almost entirely disappeared from mainstream

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:21.020
Hollywood.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:21.800
Here’s why.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:23.120
Leading the trail

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:28.000
Despite his hasty retreat from the acting
spotlight, Norton has kept himself busy on

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.720
the production side of the film industry.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:35.300
Since 2015, he's been listed as a producer
on Lewis &amp; Clark, a long-awaited HBO miniseries

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:39.060
about the two famous explorers who trekked
through the Louisiana Purchase at the dawn

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.190
of the 19th century.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.340
“It’s taken a long time getting it all
together but we finally ready and we're starting

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:46.280
to shoot it this summer”

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:50.240
Unfortunately, filming on Lewis &amp; Clark shut
down after only two months.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:54.540
Thanks to an array of further production issues,
the series still has no release date.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:55.960
Calling the shots

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:00.620
In over 20 years in Hollywood, Norton has
only directed one movie: Keeping the Faith,

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:04.879
a 2000 rom-com about a Catholic priest and
a rabbi fighting over the woman they both

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:05.380
love.

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:09.240
Norton has recently returned to the director’s
chair, however, with Motherless Brooklyn,

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:12.820
a 50s crime drama adapted from the novel of
the same name.

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:17.020
Perhaps unsurprisingly, Motherless Brooklyn
has been the subject of some controversy.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:22.240
A fire on location destroyed an apartment
in March 2018, leading to a lawsuit against

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:26.020
Norton’s production company for “recklessness,
carelessness and negligence.”

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:30.700
The same blaze also claimed the life of firefighter
Michael Davidson, whose family subsequently

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:32.960
issued a wrongful death lawsuit against the
company.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:34.840
Working behind the scenes

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:40.400
One of Norton's more recent roles came thanks
to Seth Rogen's animated movie Sausage Party,

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:45.670
in which Norton voiced Sammy Bagel Jr. an
anthropomorphised bagel who sounds suspiciously

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:46.500
like Woody Allen.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:50.080
Both the character and his familiar-sounding
voice was Norton's idea.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:57.800
“Can we all just calm calm down a notch,
try to be amicable, I'm Sammy Bagel Jr.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:59.820
I'm happy to meet all of you.”

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:01.460
Rogen told Deadline,

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:05.509
"He really latched onto it, and was a huge
proponent of it, and said from the very beginning

00:02:05.509 --> 00:02:08.030
that he wanted to play a bagel that sounded
like Woody Allen.”

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:12.319
Norton was also instrumental in getting Sausage
Party made in the first place, encouraging

00:02:12.319 --> 00:02:16.400
Rogen and his collaborator Evan Goldberg to
stick it out when the going got tough and

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.840
convincing other big stars to voice characters
in the movie including Kristen Wiig and Salma

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:21.340
Hayek.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:22.600
A major bomb

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:27.360
Norton's most recent major role came in 2016’s
Collateral Beauty.

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:31.280
Despite a stellar cast and some pre-release
Oscar buzz, however, the movie flopped hard

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:36.650
at the box office, earning a measly $31 million
in the U.S. largely because it shared a release

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:37.640
date with Rogue One.

00:02:37.849 --> 00:02:41.760
Critics panned the movie too, and Collateral
Beauty ended up failing to provide the comeback

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.320
vehicle for Norton that it so easily could
have been.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:45.740
Family focus

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.440
Though he's usually pretty cagey about publicly
discussing his personal life, Norton has opened

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:53.300
up to the Independent about his decision to
ease up on acting.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:57.640
He cited his personal and family life as a
reason for this, highlighting the need to

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:00.180
strike a balance between acting and what he
called:

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.810
"[...] other things that are really compelling
or interesting or challenging to a different

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.720
part of your brain or your personality."

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:09.140
The conversation soon turned to Norton’s
view of the film industry as a whole.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:09.780
He said:

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:14.040
"I just think that I'm less interested than
I used to be in, like, exploring genre for

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:14.620
the sake of it.”

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:19.040
He went on to explain that he prefers to take
roles in movies which are innovative or unique,

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:23.720
or are helmed by particular filmmakers he
respects such as Spike Lee or Wes Anderson.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:25.920
Doesn’t quite explain Sausage Party, though.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:27.420
Roasting Marvel

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:32.720
In 2018, Norton made a rare televised appearance
as a guest at the Comedy Central Roast of

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:33.460
Bruce Willis.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:37.240
Naturally, Norton made some harsh jabs towards
his Moonrise Kingdom co-star.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:41.540
But much of Norton's routine appeared to simply
be a set-up to attack Norton’s true nemesis:

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:42.720
Marvel, saying,

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.100
"I did a big action movie called The Incredible
Hulk.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:48.160
[...] I thought we should try to make one
Marvel movie that was as good as the worst

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.420
Chris Nolan movie, but what the hell was I
thinking?"

